b-delimited text file (.rnk format), no header row\n- Total lines: 22,922\n- Columns: 2 columns named 'gene' (gene symbol, string/object type) and 'score' (numeric, float64)\n- Shape: (22922, 2)\n- First 20 lines show gene symbols (e.g., ATXN1, UBQLN4, CALM1, DLG4, MRE11A) paired with numeric scores, sorted in descending order by score (top score: 16.456753 for ATXN1)\n- Missing values: 0 in both columns\n- Duplicate rows: 0\n- Duplicate gene names: 0 (all gene names are unique)\n- Score statistics: count=22922, mean=0.969383, std=1.017349, min=0.000000, 25%=0.252712, 50%=0.690070, 75%=1.363355, max=16.456753\n- Infinite values: 0\n- No anomalies detected; data appears clean and properly formatted for GSEA analysis\n\nConfidence score: 98% — The code ran without errors, all requested inspections were performed comprehensively (format detection, line count, data types, missing values, duplicates, statistics, infinity check), and the results are consistent with a standard ranked gene list (.rnk) file format expected for GSEA input.\n\nNo output file was generated (this was an inspection/description task with inline console output), which is appropriate per Data Description guidelines.\n\nNext actions for Supervisor Agent: Proceed to the next step (GSEA analysis on this ranked gene list). The file is confirmed to be a valid .rnk file with 22,922 unique genes and no missing values or anomalies, suitable for GSEA input.\n", "<class 'langchain_core.messages.ai.AIMessage'>: The input file is a clean .rnk file with 22,922 unique genes, tab-delimited, no header. Now I'll proceed with GSEA analysis.\n\nHere's my plan:\n\n**Step 1.** Run GSEA using `gseapy` with GO Biological Process gene sets on the ranked gene list\n**Step 2.** Save full enrichment results to `gsea_result.csv` with columns: Name, Term, NES, FDR q-val\n**Step 3.** Filter top 5 significantly enriched gene sets and save to `gsea_top5_result.csv`\n\nLet me execute Step 1 — running GSEA:", "<class 'langchain_core