ult_714/toolsgenie_20260714/data/gsea_result.csv (CSV format, 2654 rows, columns: Name, Term, ES, NES, NOM p-val, FDR q-val, FWER p-val)\n- Top 5 results: /mnt/data/lengyang/youjia_project/autoba/BABench/src/promptbio-bench/tasks/a-2-8/result_714/toolsgenie_20260714/data/gsea_top5_result.csv (CSV format, 5 rows)\n- GSEA output directory: /mnt/data/lengyang/youjia_project/autoba/BABench/src/promptbio-bench/tasks/a-2-8/result_714/toolsgenie_20260714/data/gsea_output\n\nConfidence score: 97% — The code ran without errors, all specified parameters were correctly used, output files were generated with required columns (Name, Term, NES, FDR q-val), sorting was verified correct (FDR q-val ascending, then absolute NES descending), and results are biologically meaningful. The 3% deduction accounts for the informational warning about duplicated gene scores which could marginally affect gene ordering.\n\nNext actions for Supervisor Agent: Proceed to the next step. The GSEA analysis completed successfully with valid outputs. Both gsea_result.csv and gsea_top5_result.csv have been generated as required.\n", "<class 'langchain_core.messages.ai.AIMessage'>: GSEA analysis completed successfully. Let me verify the output files to ensure they meet the requirements:", "<class 'langchain_core.messages.tool.ToolMessage'>: Response: \nThe verification task executed successfully without errors. The code read both CSV files, printed their shapes, columns, and content, and confirmed the presence of all required columns (Name, Term, NES, FDR q-val) in both files.\n\nReview methodology: I verified the code against the 14 common error rules. (1) File paths are correct and both files exist (code executed successfully). (2) No encoding issues with default UTF-8. (3-7) Not applicable as this is a read-only verification task with no computation or grouping. (8) Data format is valid CSV. (9) No function parameters used beyond pd.read_csv defaults. (10) All variables defined before use. (11) pandas 