ion Summary\n\n**Input:** `gene_rnk.txt` — a ranked gene list with 22,922 unique genes (tab-delimited, no header)\n\n**Method:** GSEA via `gseapy.prerank()` using GO Biological Process 2023 gene sets, 1,000 permutations, min gene set size 15, max 500, seed=42.\n\n## Results\n\n**Full enrichment results** (`gsea_result.csv`): 2,654 gene sets tested, with columns: Name, Term, ES, NES, NOM p-val, FDR q-val, FWER p-val. Sorted by FDR q-val ascending, then |NES| descending.\n\n**Top 5 significantly enriched gene sets** (`gsea_top5_result.csv`):\n\n| # | Term | NES | FDR q-val |\n|---|------|-----|-----------|\n| 1 | Cytoplasmic Translation (GO:0002181) | 1.836 | 0.003 |\n| 2 | Response To Epidermal Growth Factor (GO:0070849) | 1.740 | 0.003 |\n| 3 | Positive Regulation Of Leukocyte Proliferation (GO:0070665) | 1.741 | 0.004 |\n| 4 | Fc Receptor Signaling Pathway (GO:0038093) | 1.737 | 0.004 |\n| 5 | Negative Regulation Of Synaptic Transmission (GO:0050805) | 1.742 | 0.004 |\n\nAll top 5 gene sets are highly significant (FDR q-val < 0.005) with strong positive enrichment (NES > 1.7), indicating upregulation of these biological processes in the ranked gene list.\n\n### Plan Checklist\n- [✓] **Step 1.** Run GSEA using `gseapy.prerank()` with GO Biological Process gene sets on the ranked gene list\n- [✓] **Step 2.** Save full enrichment results to `gsea_result.csv` with required columns (Name, Term, NES, FDR q-val)\n- [✓] **Step 3.** Filter top 5 significantly enriched gene sets and save to `gsea_top5_result.csv`\n- [✓] **Step 4.** Verify both output files contain required columns and valid data\n\n### Output Files\n- **`gsea_result.csv`** — 2,654 rows × 7 columns (full GSEA results)\n- **`gsea_top5_result.csv`** — 5 rows × 7 columns (top 5 enriched gene sets)"], 'input_token_num': 49588, 'output_token_num': 14334}
